hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1129","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi narrated to us, Bishr, meaning Ibn Bakr, narrated to us, on the authority of al-Awza’i, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, H, and he narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Alil al-Muqri, and Ahmad ibn Issa ibn Yazid al-Lakhmi al-Tannisi, said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Hakam bin Thawban, Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not be like so-and-so. \Night.\"" Yunus said: The Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: “O Abdullah"," do not be.”"""
